ion is why do we  use columns in the first place  the magnetic separators and column-based  and column-free systems have a  comparable magnetic force  but the difference between the systems  is the column  this column is filled with small iron  spheres  each iron sphere passes the magnetic  force on to the next over a very small  distance thus amplifying the magnetic  force by ten thousand fold and ensuring  that the magnetic field is constant  throughout the column  this system allows for the minimal  labeling of cells with microbeads to  retain the target cells in the column  without relying on epitope saturation or  large beads that can interfere with  downstream applications such as cell  culture or flow cytometric analysis  the iron spheres have a cell friendly  coating that allows for the cells to run  freely through the column and can be  washed thoroughly to remove cell debris  and contaminants  all of this contributes to the fact that  max columns allow for highly effective  cell separation with minimal effects on  cells  if you would like to learn more about  the technology itself its benefits and  to see some data feel free to have a  look at the webinar recording select the  best with max technology on our website  the link will also be included in the  recording of this webinar or just search  cell separation in the video library on  our website  by leveraging the advantages of max  technology  we have developed a number of kits for  the isolation of nk cells t-regs and  macrophages from both human and mice  and while i won't go into the details of  these various kits you can rest assured  that we have the products and solutions  for the isolation of these key cell  types for most any researcher  when it comes to isolating cells  you can choose the cell separation  option or options according to your  needs  whether it's a manual process for a  limited number of samples all the way up  to a fully automated high throughput  cell separation instrument  mi