ion is why do we  use columns in the first place  the magnetic separators and column-based  and column-free systems have a  comparable magnetic force  but the difference between the systems  is the column  this column is filled with small iron  spheres  each iron sphere passes the magnetic  force on to the next over a very small  distance thus amplifying the magnetic  force by ten thousand fold and ensuring  that the magnetic field is constant  throughout the column  this system allows for the minimal  labeling of cells with microbeads to  retain the target cells in the column  without relying on epitope saturation or  large beads that can interfere with  downstream applications such as cell  culture or flow cytometric analysis  the iron spheres have a cell friendly  coating that allows for the cells to run  freely through the column and can be  washed thoroughly to remove cell debris  and contaminants  all of this contributes to the fact that  max columns allow for highly effective  cell separation with minimal effects on  cells  if you would like to learn more about  the technology itself its benefits and  to see some data feel free to have a  look at the webinar recording select the  best with max technology on our website  the link will also be included in the  recording of this webinar or just search  cell separation in the video library on  our website  by leveraging the advantages of max  technology  we have developed a number of kits for  the isolation of nk cells t-regs and  macrophages from both human and mice  and while i won't go into the details of  these various kits you can rest assured  that we have the products and solutions  for the isolation of these key cell  types for most any researcher  when it comes to isolating cells  you can choose the cell separation  option or options according to your  needs  whether it's a manual process for a  limited number of samples all the way up  to a fully automated high throughput  cell separation instrument  miltoni biotech has you covered  now  while manual cell separation certainly  has its place in  certain day-to-day operations  our focus now is on automation  but why do we actually need automation  what is the advantage  automation reduces hands-on time and  frees you up to work on other tasks in  the meantime  tasks that cannot be automated  it minimizes variation between different  users in the lab or even good and bad  days of an individual scientist  and of course it minimizes costly human  errors  with standard protocols and minimal user  variation you can be sure that the  effects that you're seeing  are due to your assay rather than  artifacts  in short automation reduces redundant  experiments and allows you to focus your  time where it matters  there are two instruments that i would  like to highlight at this point  if you're interested in isolating  multiple samples in parallel the  multi-max family is a perfect fit for  this  24 magnets allow you to process between  1 and 24 samples in one run  or split your large sample between  multiple columns  this is achieved by using the ls ld or  whole blood columns  or the multi 24 column block for the  easy handling of 24 samples or one very  large sample like an entire leukopak  the multi-max 24 is a semi-automated  instrument and a good fit for many labs  that value easy handling but don't mind  manual pipetting  however  if you want full automation and maximum  throughput you'll love the multi-max x  which integrates a multi-max into a  liquid handling system  as mentioned the multi-max x is the  instrument for the high demanding high  throughput cell processing lab  samples are labeled and isolated  automatically  both for pvmc generation or  cell subpopulations from tumor samples  all programs are tailored to match your  needs so we don't leave the lab until  you're satisfied with the protocol and  the results  for many researchers  once you have isolated your cells of  interest the real work begins  this often starts with the culturing of  target populations for downstream  functional assays  so in the next section we will talk  about our cell culture portfolio which  includes activation  expansion and functional assay products  our max cell culture and stimulation  portfolio comprises a specialized and  versatile range of cell culture media  and reagents for cell stimulation  expansion  and or differentiation  products are available for human and  mouse primary cells including immune  stem neural and tumor cells  many of these products are available in  both research and gmp quality allowing  for the smooth translation into the  clinic  first we will discuss the media options  that we have from our cell culture  portfolio  for scientists that are working with t  cells our tex-max medium has been  designed for high performance t-cell  growth  high cell viability and consistency  under serum free conditions  it has been optimized for the serum free  cultivation and expansion of human and  mouse t cells and t-rex  our tex-max medium has a defined  formulation enabling reproducible  applications in human and male cell  cultures  it is produced without animal-based  derived components but contains  pre-selected human serum albumin stable  glutamine and phenol red  our research grade medium has been  developed based on our texmax gmp medium  again allowing for the smooth  translation into the clinic  for researchers working on nk cells we  offer our nk max medium which is the  perfect solution for nk cell cultures  and expansion from pbmcs or isolated nk  cells  the chemically defined xenofree  composition ensures reproducible results  expanded nk cells are fully functional  and can be used in any downstream  application such as killing assays  if you're starting your expansion from  pvmcs  the unwanted growth and expansion of t  cells and nkt cells is minimal  for researchers that are looking to  establish primary tumor cell lines our  cancer cell culture medium is optimized  for the efficient initiation and  expansion of human tumor cell cultures  from primary and xenotransplanted tumors  with standardized serum free  formulations  our tumor max media offers optimal  conditions for the generation of primary  cell lines by enhancing cell  proliferation without inducing any  genomic changes  the cells will maintain their  heterogeneity and tumorogenic potential  improving in vitro models for cancer  research and drug screening  t-regs are often functionally analyzed  by in in vitro by a so-called  suppression assay  for this purpose t-regs are co-cultured  with t responder cells at different  ratios in the presence of a polyclonal  stimulus  t-regs alone show a hypoproliferative  response whereas g-responder cells alone  can show a proliferative response  by co-culturing t-regs with t-responder  cells you can often see a reduction in  the incorporation of either thymidine or  the dilution of the cell tracking  reagent in the t responding cells  this suppression assay is performed with  a dilution ranging from a ratio of one  to one to eight to one the responder  cells to t reg cells as outlined in the  figure below  this product allows you to evaluate the  functionality of your t-regs not just  based on phenotypic analysis of surface  markers or cytokine secretion  in this next section we will be  discussing some of the critical aspects  that need to be taken into consideration  when phenotyping your cells of interest  especially in the context of the tumor  microenvironment  some genetic mouse tumor models  represent a gold standard to analyze the  effects of immunotherapy  as they possess a fully competent immune  repertoire  such analyses routinely rely on the  characterization of tumor infiltrating  leukocytes and their phenotype  however the amount and composition of  tills is highly variable and often very  low  complicating the flow cytometric  analysis of individual subpopulations  to make things more difficult  traditional hybridoma-derived antibody  clones used for flow cytometric  evaluation of tills show a tendency of  non-specific binding to immune cells  such as myeloid cells via naturally  expressing the fc gamma receptors or  induced expression of fc gamma receptors  on t cells in the context of the tumor  microenvironment  this can lead to an inaccurate and  biased estimation of till populations  to avoid fc gamma receptor mediated  background binding blocking reagents  including commercially available  immunoglobulins are used  this adds additional complexity to the  analysis as there's no defined consensus  on the best titer and type of blocking  reagents that is supposed to be used for  complex tissues like tumors in addition  blocking reagents increase staining time  and hinder the ability to scale up or  automate multi-sample analyses  here i'm describing the benefits of  using our re-affinity recombinant  antibody clones for the analysis of  different till populations  reaffinity antibodies provide several  benefits  over hybridoma-derived antibody clones  for example a specifically mutated human  igg-1 fc region that abolishes their  ability to bind to the fce  gamma receptor  this enables more reliable and  reproducible flow cytometric analysis  so i'd like to take a brief moment to  describe a little bit about our  re-affinity antibodies  our re-affinity antibodies are  recombinant antibodies that provide  superior lot to lot consistency and  purity compared to mouse or rat  hybridoma-derived monoclonal antibodies  they have been recombinantly engineered  to produce highly specific antibodies  that require no fc blocking  and additionally  they have the same igg-1 isotec  requiring less isotype controls  the manufacturing process of re-affinity  recombinant antibodies ensures high  performance based on the following  aspects  they are derived from a defined dna  sequence which encodes only one type of  heavy and light chain ensuring high  antibody purity  production is under biologically and  chemically defined standards  that result in  high lot to lot consistency  analytical biochemical and cell-based  testing of every lot ensures you're  going to get the highest quality most  reproducible antibody possible  all reaffinity recombinant antibody  clones contain the same specifically  mutated human igg-1 sequence as their  constant region  this offers the possibility to work with  only one type of isotype reducing the  complexity of experiment planning and  saving time as well as money  hybrid  monoclonal antibodies on the other hand  are composed of antibody isotypes  derived from different species and  therefore require multiple isotype  controls  this complicates not only the management  of reagent inventory but also panel  design when setting up experiments  all reaffinity recombinant antibodies  contain a specifically mutated human  igg1 sc region which abolishes their  need to block or to bind fc gamma  receptors  this allows for background free analysis  and eliminates the need for additional  blocking steps such as using an fcr  blocking reagent  one of the product highlights that i'd  like to draw attention to in our cell  analysis portfolio is our mdsc detection  kit  now myeloid derived suppressor cells are  a heterogeneous group of mononuclear  myeloid cells with  different immunosuppressive as well as  disease-promoting functions  in healthy volunteers they're found in  relatively small numbers but can expand  considerably in pathological conditions  depending on the type and stage of  disease the mdsc population might be  present in different maturation phases  validated unambiguous phenotypic markers  for mdscs are still lacking and  therefore various combinations of  specificities are used for their  identification  the mdsc detection kit is intended to be  used for the standardization and  simplification of flow cytometric  analysis of subpopulations of mdscs  described thus far  for greater flexibility the product  configuration also allows  the extension of the analysis panel with  additional specific specificities of  interest  examples being cd10 or cd66b  the mdsc detection kit has been designed  for the detection of circulating mdscs  and cell suspensions of pvmcs  and might be used for the analysis of  other starting materials such as whole  blood lysed whole blood or single cell  suspensions from human tissues such as  tumor cells  so finally i would like to briefly  mention a few key aspects of our  translational and clinical offerings for  those that are looking to take their  research to the clinic  as an innovative biotechnology company  we at miltoni biotech offer cutting edge  technologies and high quality products  to support your immuno oncology research  whether you are interested in studying  immune cells or cancer cells from the  tumor micro environment  or cellular models for the validation of  novel immunotherapeutic agents  check out our applications page for the  respective cell types  whether they're engineered t cells for  research  macrophages or modics nk cells or tumor  infiltrating leukocytes  to find relevant application data and  protocols based on our immuno oncology  products  moreover  we offer clinical scale immuno oncology  products for the easy transition of your  research workflows into the clinic  i'd like to thank everyone for attending  this webinar and for additional  information please visit our booth here  at the lab roots immuno oncology virtual  event or our website for all the tools  and solutions needed to advance your  potentially life-saving research  thank you and keep up the good fight
 

